@* Counter.razor — stock vanilla Blazor. The framework translates
   @onclick into a data-wasp-evt-click attribute via WaspHtmlRenderer.
   State lives in CounterService (singleton, backed by stable memory)
   because the render-as-query model re-instantiates components on
   every call. *@

@inject WaspSample.BlazorWasp.CounterService CounterState

<h1>Counter</h1>

<p role="status">Current count: <span data-wasp-bind="counter:value">@CounterState.Count</span></p>

<button class="btn btn-primary" @onclick="CounterState.Increment">Click me</button>

<p style="margin-top:1.5rem; color:#8b93a7; font-size:0.85rem;">
    Live count — open this page in two browsers. Other users' clicks show up here in ~400 ms via the
    <code>/api/counter</code> Candid-style delta endpoint, not a full page re-render.
</p>
